### Transaction API Testing

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/transactions

### 1. Create a Transaction
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "amount": 100.50,
  "currency": "USD",
  "transactionType": "DEPOSIT"
}

### A. Create with a client-supplied Transaction ID
### The ID is optional. Reusing an existing ID returns 409 Conflict.
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": 1001,
  "customerId": 1,
  "amount": 100.50,
  "currency": "USD",
  "transactionType": "DEPOSIT"
}

### A. Duplicate Transaction ID (returns 409 after the request above)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "transactionId": 1001,
  "customerId": 1,
  "amount": 25.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "transactionType": "PAYMENT"
}

### 2. Create another transaction for the same customer
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "amount": 75.25,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "transactionType": "WITHDRAWAL"
}

### 3. Create transaction for different customer
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 2,
  "amount": 500.00,
  "currency": "GBP",
  "transactionType": "TRANSFER"
}

### 4. Get Transaction by ID (replace 1 with actual ID from response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/1

### B. Get a missing transaction (returns 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/99999

### 5. Get All Transactions for Customer 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/customer/1

### 6. Get All Transactions for Customer 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/customer/2

### 7. Get All Transactions
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 8. Update Transaction Status (replace 1 with actual ID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1/status?status=COMPLETED

### 9. Update to Failed Status
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1/status?status=FAILED

### 10. Update to Cancelled Status
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1/status?status=CANCELLED

### C. Invalid status transition (returns 409 after transaction 1 is terminal)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/1/status?status=FAILED

### D. Get all transactions for a customer (individual request)
GET {{baseUrl}}/customer/1

### Test Invalid Requests

### Test - Invalid Amount (0)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "amount": 0,
  "currency": "USD",
  "transactionType": "DEPOSIT"
}

### Test - Invalid Currency (too long)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "USDA",
  "transactionType": "DEPOSIT"
}

### Test - Null Customer ID
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "USD",
  "transactionType": "DEPOSIT"
}

### Test - Get Non-Existent Transaction
GET {{baseUrl}}/99999
